# `const pair = [..]; <a branch>; const [a, b] = pair;`: the list is written in one block and taken apart in another, and the block that writes it is walked more than once:
# the join once for each literal that a way brings (eachWay), the body of the loop once for each copy of the loop (behindLoop). What each walk made meets in front of the pattern, and the elements' written names are bound to nothing there.
